    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass with a green build. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the bulk-signup warning rule on `POST /api/owners`: **when more than 80 owners have already been created for an owner's registration date, the returned owner carries `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.**\n\nThe value reflects the count *at signup time* (like the existing `namesakeCount`/`customerCode`), so it's computed on create and persisted, then returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Changes:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` with the accessor).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the nullable `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column. Seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they're unaffected.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 set the warning before save via a new `computeBulkSignupWarning(...)` that counts existing owners sharing the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (the same accumulation path as the daily-limit rule) and returns `count > 80`. The owner being created is excluded since it isn't saved yet.\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the field by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests` passes, and the full suite is green: **33 run, 0 failures, 0 errors.**",
